Z||000000||EdsB52||07-27-2001||04:41 PM||||I'm doing a clutch on my 94 Z-28 and for fun placed it in my Isuzu tranny I had laying on the floor. The diameter was close, but didn't interferre. The clutch splines didn't work though. Another non-conformity was the fact that the throwout bearing actually pulls on the pressure plate fingers instead of pushing them. What a wacky set up, did some Ford engineers go to work for GM? Has anyone checked this application for potential conformity to V-8 or Northstar applications?||||reg||1
